// Develop 1.0: photo-style grading sliders and film light for DaVinci Resolve, in one DCTL.
// 0.4: the colour mixer is a hue engine in Oklab (eight control hues on the measured hues of their colours, a neutral
// guard, Skin Unify, Skin Protect, Hue Lum Evening); with every mixer slider at 0 it is the 0.3 arithmetic exactly.
// Input and output: Rec.709, gamma 2.4 (display-referred). MIT License.
//
// Use it as a ResolveFX DCTL plugin node for live sliders, or apply it as a LUT on a node
// (the sliders' default values are then used, so a copy with edited defaults is a fixed look).
// Every slider defaults to neutral, and with every effect at neutral the input is returned
// untouched, values above 1 and below 0 included.
//
// Sampling: highlight recovery, deband, mist, sparkle, halation and the three detail bands share
// one fixed pattern of 144 taps in five rings out to 4.1% of the frame height, plus the centre
// pixel. The pattern is the same for every pixel and every frame and is never randomly rotated,
// so the light effects carry no frozen noise on a LUT copy. Grain and the deband dither are
// hashed from the frame index: they move in the plugin, and on a LUT copy (frame index held at 1)
// they are a static fine pattern.
// With every effect on, a pixel reads 145 RGB taps (435 single-channel reads).
//
// Gamut compression follows the ACES Reference Gamut Compression specification (CC BY 4.0).
// The Oklab matrices are the published Oklab reference values. White balance adapts in the CAT16
// cone space of CIECAM16, with the Planckian locus from Krystek's approximation (1985).

// ---- Basic
DEFINE_UI_PARAMS(temp,     Temp,       DCTLUI_SLIDER_FLOAT, 0.0, -100.0, 100.0, 1.0)
DEFINE_UI_PARAMS(tint,     Tint,       DCTLUI_SLIDER_FLOAT, 0.0, -100.0, 100.0, 1.0)
DEFINE_UI_PARAMS(expo,     Exposure,   DCTLUI_SLIDER_FLOAT, 0.0, -4.0, 4.0, 0.01)
